# Token-Efficiency Rules

## Response style
- Be concise. No preambles, no recap of what I asked, no closing summaries.
- Don't explain code unless I ask. Show only the changed lines/diff, not whole files.
- Answer in the shortest form that is correct. No filler or pleasantries.
- Reply in the language I write in.

## Reading & context
- Don't read files unless needed for the task. Prefer targeted search (grep) over opening whole files.
- Never re-read a file you've already seen in this conversation.
- Don't scan the whole repo for small, local changes.

## Editing
- Make minimal edits. Don't refactor, rename, reformat, or "improve" code I didn't mention.
- Don't add comments, docs, or tests unless I ask.
- If the request is ambiguous, ask one short question instead of guessing and producing long output.

## Tools & agents
- Don't run commands, builds, or tests unless needed to verify the change.
- Avoid repeating failed attempts. If something fails twice, stop and tell me why.
